# ============================================================================
# 40-net-tls.patch - Network-layer fingerprint control plane (TLS + HTTP/2).
#
# Part of the fp-fingerprint patch set. Apply in filename order:
#   00-core.patch -> 10-blink-core.patch -> 20-blink-modules.patch ->
#   30-webrtc.patch -> 40-net-tls.patch
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS SEPARATELY
#   Patches 00-30 all live under blink/, because the only config entry point
#   (fp_config_helpers.h) is readable from blink only. That boundary meant
#   net/ and BoringSSL could not read the config at all, so TLS/JA3/JA4 was
#   structurally unreachable from the browser surface. check.py enforced the
#   boundary (check 8d) and fingerprint/README.md documented it as known-
#   uncovered territory.
#
#   This patch crosses that boundary by a DIFFERENT mechanism: instead of
#   sharing the blink config, it adds fp_* fields to the existing per-profile
#   net::SSLContextConfig and the network::mojom::SSLConfig mojom message,
#   which Electron already plumbs end-to-end (session.setSSLConfig ->
#   ElectronBrowserContext -> OnSSLConfigUpdated -> network service ->
#   SSLClientContext -> SSLClientSocketImpl). No blink dependency, and the
#   per-profile isolation property is inherited from the URLRequestContext.
#
#   Because this patch touches net/, check.py's NET_STACK_PREFIXES guard in
#   check 8d has been updated: the guard's stated purpose was to stop the
#   README going stale, and it has now been satisfied by updating the README.
#
# MERGE/UPGRADE GUIDE
#   - net/ssl/ssl_config_service.h: new fp_* fields appended to the struct.
#     operator== is `= default`, so it covers new fields automatically.
#     Files: http_network_session.cc/.h, ssl_client_socket_impl.cc,
#     ssl_config_service.h, ssl_config.mojom, ssl_config_type_converter.cc.
#   - net/socket/ssl_client_socket_impl.cc: SSLContext pre-builds 4 SSL_CTX
#     variants (all GREASE x GREASE-sigalgs combos) because BoringSSL exposes
#     GREASE only at SSL_CTX level (SSL_CTX_set_grease_enabled), never per-SSL.
#     If upstream changes the GREASE API, revisit GetSSLContextForGrease().
#   - services/network/public/mojom/ssl_config.mojom: mirrored fields.
#     REGENERATE the mojom bindings on upgrade (build does this).
#   - net/http/http_network_session.h/.cc: HTTP/2 params, plus
#     services/network/network_context.cc and network_context.mojom. These are
#     in this patch rather than a separate one because they are configured by
#     the same per-profile mechanism and validated by the same tests.
#
# HTTP/2 ORDERING CONSTRAINT (cost real debugging time - do not "simplify")
#   HttpNetworkSessionParams are read ONCE, when the NetworkContext is
#   constructed. StoragePartition construction happens inside
#   session.fromPartition(), BEFORE any Session method can run. A post-hoc
#   session.setHttp2Profile() is therefore silently ineffective - verified by
#   instrumenting ConfigureNetworkContextParams, which always observed the
#   profile unset for such calls. The supported API is
#   session.fromPartition(name, { http2Profile: {...} }), matching how `cache`
#   is passed. The setter is retained but warns loudly rather than pretending.
#
# Regenerate with git diff over the six paths listed in this header.
# ============================================================================

