+  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
+  // Fingerprint profile: browser-profile-driven TLS ClientHello control.
+  //
+  // These are the surfaces that Chromium otherwise HARDCODES in
+  // SSLClientSocketImpl::Init(), which is why a Chromium-derived build cannot
+  // move its JA3/JA4 without a source change. All of them default to
+  // "unset / native Chromium behavior" so that an unprofiled context is
+  // byte-identical to stock Chromium - a lie that is inconsistent with the
+  // rest of the stack is worse than no spoof at all.
+  //
+  // Design rule enforced here: these describe TLS *behavior*, not the JA3/JA4
+  // string. The hashes are DERIVED on the wire from what these produce. Never
+  // add a field that stores a target JA3/JA4 - that inverts the dependency and
+  // makes the profile unverifiable.
